---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import IsometricCity from "@/components/IsometricCity.astro";
import LumaCalendar from "@/components/LumaCalendar.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Growth Circuit"
  description="Meet the people building growth systems through public NYC events, WhatsApp groups, and a growing directory of member projects."
  hideHeader
  bodyClass="sky-page pivot-page"
>
  <div class="pivot-hero">
    <header class="pivot-header">
      <div class="shell pivot-nav">
        <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Growth Circuit home">
          <img class="brand-logo" src="/growth-circuit-icon.svg" alt="" width="44" height="44" />
          <span>Growth Circuit</span>
        </a>
        <nav class="pivot-nav__links" aria-label="Main navigation">
          <a href="/events">Events</a>
          <a href="/people">People + projects</a>
          <a href="/apply?source=nav">Apply</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="shell pivot-hero__inner">
      <div class="pivot-hero__copy">
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--live">NYC-first. Open to everyone.</p>
        <h1>Build with people who <span>get what you do.</span></h1>
        <p class="pivot-lead">Growth Circuit is a close-knit community for marketing engineers who want to share their work, sharpen their craft, and make cool sh*t together.</p>
        <div class="pivot-actions">
          <a class="button matcha" href="/events">See upcoming events →</a>
          <a class="pivot-text-link" href="#join">Join WhatsApp ↓</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <IsometricCity featuredEventUrl="/events" />
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="shell model-section" aria-labelledby="model-title">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">How the circuit works</p>
      <h2 id="model-title">Pick how you want to show up.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="model-grid">
      <article>
        <span class="model-card__number">NYC</span>
        <h3>Meet in New York</h3>
        <p>Larger events, usually 30 to 100 people, are how most people find Growth Circuit. Expect people who work on growth and have real things to share.</p>
        <a href="/events">See upcoming events →</a>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="model-card__number">Chat</span>
        <h3>Talk on WhatsApp</h3>
        <p>Between events, share what you are working on, ask a question, or pass along something useful. Join the local NYC group or the broader global group.</p>
        <a href="#join">Choose your group →</a>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="model-card__number">Work</span>
        <h3>Show what you built</h3>
        <p>We are building a public directory of members and the things they have shipped. Claim a profile, add your projects, and let your work be findable.</p>
        <a href="/people">Preview profiles →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="supper-note"><span>Small table, by invitation</span> Nick and Lucy also host smaller dinners for people they meet at larger events.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="shell calendar-section" aria-labelledby="event-title">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">On the calendar</p>
      <h2 id="event-title">Come to the next one.</h2>
      <p>Meetups in New York, online show &amp; tells, and more ways to meet the people building growth systems.</p>
    </div>
    <LumaCalendar />
  </section>

  <section class="shell profiles-feature" aria-labelledby="profiles-title">
    <div class="profiles-feature__copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Coming soon</p>
      <h2 id="profiles-title">A public home for people and their work.</h2>
      <p>Claim your Growth Circuit profile, add the projects you have shipped, and make your work findable by people who care about it. Doorway can make it easy to publish a project and attach it to your profile.</p>
      <div class="profile-labels" aria-label="Planned profile features">
        <span>Member profiles</span><span>Project pages</span><span>Curated highlights</span>
      </div>
      <a class="button matcha" href="/people">Preview the directory →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="profile-preview" aria-label="Example Growth Circuit profile">
      <div class="profile-preview__top"><span>growthcircuit.club/people/you</span><span>Claimed ✓</span></div>
      <div class="profile-preview__identity"><div class="profile-preview__avatar">YOU</div><div><p>Marketing engineer</p><h3>Your name</h3><span>New York City</span></div></div>
      <div class="profile-preview__project"><span>Latest project</span><strong>The useful thing you shipped</strong><small>Published with Doorway ↗</small></div>
      <p class="profile-preview__note">Useful WhatsApp conversations may become public highlights after review. Private conversation stays private.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="whatsapp-section" id="join" aria-labelledby="join-title">
    <div class="shell whatsapp-section__inner">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Between events</p>
        <h2 id="join-title">Keep the conversation going.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="whatsapp-section__copy">
        <p>There are two WhatsApp groups, one for New York City and one for the broader global community. Share builds, ask useful questions, and meet people working on similar problems.</p>
        <div class="whatsapp-actions">
          <a class="button matcha" href="/apply?path=nyc">Apply to the NYC group →</a>
          <a class="button" href="/apply?path=global">Apply to the global group →</a>
        </div>
        <p>After you’re approved, we’ll send the WhatsApp invite.</p>
        <p class="privacy-note"><strong>Before you join:</strong> joining is explicit opt-in, and everyone in a WhatsApp group can see member phone numbers.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
